# Used automatically when you run: npm run build
#
# The driver app MUST reach the same backend as the passenger app, otherwise a ride
# created on one server is never dispatched on the other — and an OTP encrypted by one
# instance cannot be read by the other. Both apps now target the SAME LAN host
# (http://192.168.1.16:5001). The previous value (https://cab-backend-o3sg.onrender.com)
# was a stale deployment running older socket code, so rideRequest never arrived. If the
# PC's Wi-Fi IP changes: run `ipconfig`, update this file AND user-app/.env.production,
# then rebuild + sync both: npm run build && npx cap sync android. On a real release,
# restore the deployed HTTPS URL (and make sure passenger + driver both point at that
# same deployment).
VITE_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.15:5001
VITE_SOCKET_URL=http://192.168.1.15:5001

VITE_UPI_HANDLE=merchant@upi
VITE_UPI_PAYEE_NAME=RideEasy
